IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`

-- Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation.
-- LAYER 1, MODULE 3: THE FIRST SCHEDULE (scope of sections 2 to 4 and 7) AND THE SECOND SCHEDULE
-- (guidelines for the application of the reasonableness test).
--
-- READING A RESULT (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  The functions here are
-- named for the thing the Schedule limits ("sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract").
--   * JUST FALSE : the Schedule says, in its own words, that the section does NOT extend;
--   * JUST TRUE  : the Schedule says, in its own words, that it DOES extend;
--   * NOTHING    : not covered: the Schedule is silent, lists without closing, or the case falls
--                  outside what its own wording limits (a "where", a named kind of contract, or
--                  an exception such as "except in favour of a person dealing as consumer").
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `First Schedule - scope of sections 2 to 4 and 7`

-- Heading of the First Schedule: "Section 1(2)" / "SCOPE OF SECTIONS 2 TO 4 AND 7".  Not operative
-- (the cross-reference to s 1(2) and the Schedule's title); the exceptions are the paragraphs below.

-- src:543 | 1. Sections 2 to 4 do not extend to —
-- src:545 | (a) any contract of insurance (including a contract to pay an annuity on
-- src:546 | human life);
-- src:548 | (b) any contract so far as it relates to the creation or transfer of an interest
-- src:549 | in land, or to the termination of such an interest, whether by extinction,
-- src:550 | merger, surrender, forfeiture or otherwise;
-- src:552 | (c) any contract so far as it relates to the creation or transfer of a right or
-- src:553 | interest in any patent, trade mark, copyright, registered design,
-- src:554 | technical or commercial information or other intellectual property,
-- src:555 | or relates to the termination of any such right or interest;
-- src:556 | 2020 Ed. Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 13
-- src:558 | FIRST SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:560 | (d) any contract so far as it relates —
-- src:562 | (i) to the formation or dissolution of a company (which means any
-- src:563 | body corporate or unincorporated association and includes a
-- src:564 | partnership); or
-- src:566 | (ii) to its constitution or the rights or obligations of its corporators
-- src:567 | or members; and
-- src:569 | (e) any contract so far as it relates to the creation or transfer of securities or
-- src:570 | of any right or interest in securities.
@ref First Schedule para 1 (src:543-570)
GIVEN matter IS A `What the contract relates to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 1 sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) any contract of insurance (including a contract to pay an annuity on human life)" -- "Sections 2 to 4 do not extend to"
    WHEN `Insurance, including a contract to pay an annuity on human life` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) any contract so far as it relates to the creation or transfer of an interest in land, or to the termination of such an interest" -- "Sections 2 to 4 do not extend to"
    WHEN `The creation, transfer or termination of an interest in land` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) any contract so far as it relates to the creation or transfer of a right or interest in any patent, trade mark, copyright, registered design, technical or commercial information or other intellectual property, or relates to the termination of any such right or interest" -- "Sections 2 to 4 do not extend to"
    WHEN `The creation, transfer or termination of a right or interest in intellectual property` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) any contract so far as it relates (i) to the formation or dissolution of a company ...; or (ii) to its constitution or the rights or obligations of its corporators or members" -- "Sections 2 to 4 do not extend to"
    WHEN `The formation or dissolution of a company, or its constitution or the rights or obligations of its corporators or members` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) any contract so far as it relates to the creation or transfer of securities or of any right or interest in securities" -- "Sections 2 to 4 do not extend to"
    WHEN `The creation or transfer of securities, or of a right or interest in securities` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): para 1 says what sections 2 to 4 do not extend to; it does not say they extend to any other contract, and it does not mention section 7
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:562 | (i) to the formation or dissolution of a company (which means any
-- src:563 | body corporate or unincorporated association and includes a
-- src:564 | partnership); or
@ref First Schedule para 1(d)(i), "company" (src:562-564)
GIVEN entity IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 1(d)(i) the entity is a company` MEANS
    CONSIDER entity
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "a company (which means any body corporate or unincorporated association and includes a partnership)"
    WHEN `A body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `An unincorporated association` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `A partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "company ... means any body corporate or unincorporated association" -- a definition that "means"; any other entity is not a company for para 1(d)
    WHEN `Something else` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:572 | 2. Section 2(1) extends to —
-- src:574 | (a) any contract of marine salvage or towage;
-- src:576 | (b) any charterparty of a ship or hovercraft; and
@ref First Schedule para 2, first sentence (src:572-576)
GIVEN matter IS A `What the contract relates to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 2 section 2(1) extends to the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "(a) any contract of marine salvage or towage" -- "Section 2(1) extends to"
    WHEN `Marine salvage or towage` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "(b) any charterparty of a ship or hovercraft" -- "Section 2(1) extends to"
    WHEN `A charterparty of a ship or hovercraft` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "(c) any contract for the carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft" -- "Section 2(1) extends to"
    WHEN `The carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): para 2 says what section 2(1) extends to; it does not say it extends to nothing else (para 1 and para 4 say what it does not extend to)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:572 | 2. Section 2(1) extends to —
-- src:574 | (a) any contract of marine salvage or towage;
-- src:576 | (b) any charterparty of a ship or hovercraft; and
-- src:578 | (c) any contract for the carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft,
-- src:580 | but subject to this, sections 2 to 4 and 7 do not extend to any such contract except
-- src:581 | in favour of a person dealing as consumer.
@ref First Schedule para 2, second part (src:572-581)
GIVEN matter IS A `What the contract relates to`
      `in favour of a person dealing as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 2 sections 2 to 4 and 7, subject to section 2(1), extend to the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `Marine salvage or towage` THEN `para 2 bar` `in favour of a person dealing as consumer`
    WHEN `A charterparty of a ship or hovercraft` THEN `para 2 bar` `in favour of a person dealing as consumer`
    WHEN `The carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft` THEN `para 2 bar` `in favour of a person dealing as consumer`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "any such contract", that is a contract of marine salvage or towage, a charterparty or a contract for carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `para 2 bar` consumer MEANS
            IF consumer
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in favour of a person dealing as consumer" -- the exception is met, so the bar does not apply and the paragraph grants nothing (QA: a lifted bar grants nothing)
            THEN NOTHING
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sections 2 to 4 and 7 do not extend to any such contract except in favour of a person dealing as consumer" -- not in favour of a consumer
            ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:583 | 3. Where goods are carried by ship or hovercraft in pursuance of a contract
-- src:584 | which either —
-- src:586 | (a) specifies that as the means of carriage over part of the journey to be
-- src:587 | covered; or
-- src:589 | (b) makes no provision as to the means of carriage and does not exclude
-- src:590 | that means,
-- src:592 | then sections 2(2), 3 and 4 do not, except in favour of a person dealing as
-- src:593 | consumer, extend to the contract as it operates for and in relation to the carriage of
-- src:594 | the goods by that means.
@ref First Schedule para 3 (src:583-594)
GIVEN scope IS A `Scope facts`
      `in favour of a person dealing as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3 sections 2(2), 3 and 4 extend to the contract as it operates for the carriage of the goods by ship or hovercraft` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `goods are carried by ship or hovercraft`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where goods are carried by ship or hovercraft in pursuance of a contract" -- the goods are not so carried; the paragraph says nothing about whether the sections extend (the "where" conditions a negative statement, so the answer is not FALSE; see NOTES.md, fork Q-where-negative)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `either limb is met`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a contract which either (a) specifies that as the means of carriage over part of the journey ...; or (b) makes no provision as to the means of carriage and does not exclude that means" -- neither limb is met
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the term operates for the carriage`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the contract as it operates for and in relation to the carriage of the goods by that means" -- the term is outside that operation
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `in favour of a person dealing as consumer`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in favour of a person dealing as consumer" -- the exception is met (QA: a lifted bar grants nothing)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then sections 2(2), 3 and 4 do not, except in favour of a person dealing as consumer, extend to the contract as it operates for and in relation to the carriage of the goods by that means"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `goods are carried by ship or hovercraft` MEANS scope's `goods are carried by ship or hovercraft under the contract`
        `either limb is met` MEANS
                scope's `the contract specifies ship or hovercraft as the means of carriage over part of the journey`
            OR  scope's `the contract makes no provision as to the means of carriage and does not exclude ship or hovercraft`
        `the term operates for the carriage` MEANS scope's `the term operates for and in relation to the carriage of the goods by ship or hovercraft`

-- src:596 | 4. Subsections (1) and (2) of section 2 do not extend to a contract of
-- src:597 | employment, except in favour of the employee.
@ref First Schedule para 4 (src:596-597)
GIVEN matter IS A `What the contract relates to`
      `in favour of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 4 section 2(1) and (2) extend to the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN Employment THEN
        IF `in favour of the employee`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in favour of the employee" -- the exception is met (QA: a lifted bar grants nothing)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) of section 2 do not extend to a contract of employment, except in favour of the employee" -- not in favour of the employee
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): para 4 is about "a contract of employment"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Second Schedule - guidelines for application of reasonableness test`

-- Heading of the Second Schedule: "Section 11(2)" / "GUIDELINES FOR APPLICATION OF REASONABLENESS TEST".
-- Not operative.

-- src:608 | The matters to which regard is to be had in particular for the purposes of
-- src:609 | sections 6(3) and 7(3) and (4) are any of the following which appear to be relevant:
-- src:611 | (a) the strength of the bargaining positions of the parties relative to each
-- src:612 | other, taking into account (among other things) alternative means by
-- src:613 | which the customer’s requirements could have been met;
-- src:615 | (b) whether the customer received an inducement to agree to the term, or
-- src:616 | in accepting it had an opportunity of entering into a similar contract
-- src:617 | with other persons, but without having to accept a similar term;
-- src:619 | (c) whether the customer knew or ought reasonably to have known of the
-- src:620 | existence and extent of the term (having regard, among other things, to
-- src:621 | any custom of the trade and any previous course of dealing between the
-- src:622 | parties);
-- src:624 | (d) where the term excludes or restricts any relevant liability if some
-- src:625 | condition is not complied with, whether it was reasonable at the time of
-- src:626 | the contract to expect that compliance with that condition would be
-- src:627 | practicable;
-- src:629 | (e) whether the goods were manufactured, processed or adapted to the
-- src:630 | special order of the customer.
@ref Second Schedule (a) to (e) (src:608-630)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Guideline`
`sch 2 the guidelines` MEANS
    LIST
        `Bargaining positions and alternative means of meeting the customer's requirements`
        , `Inducement, or an opportunity to contract elsewhere without a similar term`
        , `Whether the customer knew or ought reasonably to have known of the term`
        , `Whether compliance with a condition was practicable`
        , `Whether the goods were made, processed or adapted to the customer's special order`

-- src:611 | (a) the strength of the bargaining positions of the parties relative to each
-- src:612 | other, taking into account (among other things) alternative means by
-- src:613 | which the customer’s requirements could have been met;
-- src:615 | (b) whether the customer received an inducement to agree to the term, or
-- src:616 | in accepting it had an opportunity of entering into a similar contract
-- src:617 | with other persons, but without having to accept a similar term;
-- src:619 | (c) whether the customer knew or ought reasonably to have known of the
-- src:620 | existence and extent of the term (having regard, among other things, to
-- src:621 | any custom of the trade and any previous course of dealing between the
-- src:622 | parties);
-- src:624 | (d) where the term excludes or restricts any relevant liability if some
-- src:625 | condition is not complied with, whether it was reasonable at the time of
-- src:626 | the contract to expect that compliance with that condition would be
-- src:627 | practicable;
-- src:629 | (e) whether the goods were manufactured, processed or adapted to the
-- src:630 | special order of the customer.
@ref Second Schedule (a) to (e), the paragraph letters (src:611-630)
GIVEN guideline IS A `Guideline`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 2 the paragraph that states the guideline` MEANS
    CONSIDER guideline
    WHEN `Bargaining positions and alternative means of meeting the customer's requirements` THEN "(a)"
    WHEN `Inducement, or an opportunity to contract elsewhere without a similar term` THEN "(b)"
    WHEN `Whether the customer knew or ought reasonably to have known of the term` THEN "(c)"
    WHEN `Whether compliance with a condition was practicable` THEN "(d)"
    WHEN `Whether the goods were made, processed or adapted to the customer's special order` THEN "(e)"

-- src:608 | The matters to which regard is to be had in particular for the purposes of
-- src:609 | sections 6(3) and 7(3) and (4) are any of the following which appear to be relevant:
@ref Second Schedule, opening words (src:608-609)
GIVEN `the determination is for the purposes of section 6(3), 7(3) or 7(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter appears to be relevant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 regard is to be had in particular to the guideline` MEANS
    IF NOT `the determination is for the purposes of section 6(3), 7(3) or 7(4)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of sections 6(3) and 7(3) and (4)" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the matter appears to be relevant`
        -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "The matters to which regard is to be had in particular ... are any of the following which appear to be relevant"
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which appear to be relevant" -- a matter that does not appear relevant is not one of those matters
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether a matter "appear[s] to be relevant" is a judgment the Schedule leaves to the court
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
